{"schema_version": 2, "model": "google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview", "effort": "medium", "params": {"n": 96, "q": 257}, "seed": 584198414, "solved": "failed", "parsed": true, "verify_ok": false, "verify_reason": "agent 1 is not balanced (exact discrepancy -772/257)", "reply": "To find the exact cut coordinates $z_0, \\dots, z_{95}$, we need to set the value obtained by each agent from the positive label portions equal to the value obtained from the negative label portions. \n\nThe divisible object is partitioned by cuts into alternating positive and negative labels. For each slot $j \\in \\{0, \\dots, 95\\}$, the interval $[3j+1, 3j+2]$ has uniform density $C=1$ (or $2C=2$ for the agent's special slot). The cut $t_j = 3j + 3/2 + (-1)^j z_j/2$ occurs exactly in this slot. The net value (positive minus negative) contributed by slot $j$ to an agent with density $C$ is exactly $-z_j \\cdot C$.\n\nEach agent also has an asymmetric piece outside the slots: density $L=195$ on $[3g, 3g+1]$ and $R$ on $[3g+2, 3g+3]$. The label on $[3g, 3g+1]$ is positive if $g$ is even and negative if $g$ is odd, and the reverse for $[3g+2, 3g+3]$. Thus, the net value from the guard intervals is $(-1)^g (L - R)$.\n\nEquating the total positive value and total negative value means the net value must be zero. Let $S = \\sum_{j=0}^{95} z_j$. For the agent whose special slot is $s$, the net equation is:\n$$(-1)^g (L - R) - S - z_s = 0 \\implies z_s + S = (-1)^g \\left(195 - R\\right)$$\n\nLet $k_s = (-1)^g (195 - R)$. Summing this equation over all $s = 0, \\dots, 95$ yields:\n$$S + 96S = \\sum_{s=0}^{95} k_s \\implies S = \\frac{1}{97} \\sum_{s=0}^{95} k_s$$\nOnce $S$ is found, we compute each $z_s = k_s - S$. \n\nBy reading the given $R$ values and applying the formulas:\nFor example, for agent A26 (guard $g=82$ (even), special $s=0$):\n$$k_0 = 195 - \\frac{50615}{257} = \\frac{195 \\times 257 - 50615}{257} = \\frac{50115 - 50615}{257} = -\\frac{500}{257}$$\nComputing $k_s$ for all 96 agents and summing them up, we get $\\sum k_s = -\\frac{36181}{257}$.\nDividing by 97 gives the sum $S = -\\frac{373}{257}$. \nThen each coordinate is computed precisely as $z_s = k_s - \\left(-\\frac{373}{257}\\right) = \\frac{k_s \\times 257 + 373}{257}$.\n\n<answer>-127/257, 127/257, 184/257, 220/257, -93/257, -22/257, 140/257, -179/257, 90/257, -142/257, -94/257, 201/257, -107/257, -54/257, -178/257, 254/257, -213/257, -109/257, -164/257, 248/257, 15/257, -117/257, 148/257, 171/257, -88/257, -173/257, -20/257, -36/257, -192/257, -40/257, -50/257, 181/257, 123/257, 119/257, -13/257, -243/257, -2/257, 33/257, 2/257, -14/257, -34/257, 242/257, 228/257, 78/257, -26/257, -144/257, 36/257, 209/257, -131/257, -99/257, -208/257, 24/257, 28/257, -157/257, -227/257, 216/257, 20/257, 199/257, -181/257, -79/257, 159/257, 9/257, 144/257, 202/257, 23/257, -202/257, -86/257, 233/257, 114/257, 178/257, -254/257, -163/257, -77/257, -225/257, -145/257, -186/257, 110/257, -15/257, 249/257, 85/257, -33/257, 205/257, 65/257, -147/257, -236/257, -38/257, 8/257, 251/257, 214/257, -177/257, 66/257, -205/257, 108/257, -170/257, -187/257, -30/257</answer>", "error": null, "elapsed_sec": 81.01, "http_status": 200, "finish_reason": "stop", "preset": "hard", "escalation_round": 2}
{"schema_version": 2, "model": "google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview", "effort": "medium", "params": {"n": 96, "q": 4113}, "seed": 455337226, "solved": "solved", "parsed": true, "verify_ok": true, "verify_reason": "ok", "reply": "To find the exact cut coordinates, we can set up an equation for each agent. The agents each have a density of 1 on every slot $j \\in \\{0, \\dots, 95\\}$, and a density of $2$ on their specifically designated special slot $s$. Outside the slots, they have a density $L$ on the interval $[3g, 3g+1]$ and $R$ on $[3g+2, 3g+3]$. \n\nFor an agent with guard $g$ and special slot $s$, the label of the interval $[3g, 3g+1]$ is $(-1)^g$ and $[3g+2, 3g+3]$ is $(-1)^{g+1}$.\nThe chosen cuts $t_j = 3j + 3/2 + (-1)^j z_j/2$ are designed precisely such that the net difference between the agent's value on the positive label pieces and the negative label pieces on slot $j$ equals exactly $z_j$. \nTherefore, if an agent evaluates the total labeled pieces, the net value (which must equal $0$ for perfect consensus-halving) simplifies to:\n$$ (-1)^g L + (-1)^{g+1} R + \\sum_{j=0}^{95} z_j + z_s = 0 $$\nLet $S = \\sum_{j=0}^{95} z_j$, and let $D_g = (-1)^g (R - L)$. Then the requirement becomes $S + z_s = D_g$.\nWe sum this relation over all 96 agents (and thus over all slots since the special slots $s$ are a permutation of $0$ to $95$):\n$$ 96S + \\sum_{s=0}^{95} z_s = \\sum_{g=0}^{95} D_g \\implies 97S = \\sum_{g=0}^{95} D_g $$\nWe evaluate this by substituting $L = 195 = 802035/4113$ and the respective values for $R$ scaled to have a common denominator of $q=4113$. Computing $D_g$ for each agent, summing them, and dividing by 97 gives exactly $S = -20579 / 4113$.\n\nFinally, we substitute $S$ back into the per-agent equation to find each $z_s$:\n$$ z_s = D_g - S $$\n\nCalculating $z_s$ for every $s$ sequentially from 0 to 95 yields the rational values requested:\n\n<answer>2514/4113, -3054/4113, -502/4113, -2657/4113, 787/4113, 1873/4113, 205/4113, 4055/4113, -288